rezono 0
pack subsidy-scheme

rules scheme
  | // Which amounts stand on a decision in force. A scheme parameter names the decision that set it; whether
  | // that decision is in force on a reference date is std-decision's rule `in_force_on` (it took effect, has
  | // not ended and is not replaced). So this conclusion rests on the decision's validity, never on its state.
  | 
  | // A parameter whose decision is in force on the reference date.
  | .decl decided_parameter(parameter: symbol, decision: symbol, on: symbol)
  | decided_parameter(p, d, r) :- scheme_parameter__decision(p, d), in_force_on(d, r).
  | 
  | .decl has_decision_in_force(parameter: symbol, on: symbol)
  | has_decision_in_force(p, r) :- decided_parameter(p, _, r).
  | 
  | // Finding: a parameter whose decision is not in force on the reference date. The facts of the scheme have
  | // none. A supposition has: its decision is only proposed (scenario 4), so an award computed from a
  | // supposed amount is never mistaken for one the council decided. It does not block.
  | .decl undecided_parameter(parameter: symbol, on: symbol)
  | undecided_parameter(p, r) :- scheme_parameter(p), reference_date(r), !has_decision_in_force(p, r).
  | 
  | .output decided_parameter, undecided_parameter
